{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of the enrollment stop at head 73706bde, tree 0ee64efe, for request a34e2978 and review request fd776bad. Verdict: CHANGES REQUESTED, for one sentence in two documents and one permission fix on the evidence. The code and tests need no change, so this needs no new gate.\n\n## Changes I request\n\n1. \"A recheck signs and submits nothing\" overstates it, in `runbook.md` and in the note. The code's own comment has it right: no act. Each `issue` call builds a new `membershipHandle` through `readerFor`, so a recheck can sign a read-session request under `artroom-session-request-1`. It also runs `persist` when a stage settles, which writes the owner's private chain. Neither is an act, and neither is a problem. Say: a recheck signs and submits no act, it may open a read session, and it may record a settled stage in the owner's private records. Up to 11 session requests from one enrollment sit under the limit of 64 per key.\n\n2. The unit `2026-10-31-enrol-stop`, which the note calls sealed, has 28 writable files of 28. `SHA256SUMS` reruns clean with digest 0e7b7f58, so nothing has changed. Make the files read-only. That changes no digest and needs no new head. Say so in the next request.\n\n## Your five points\n\n1. Yes, that wording is right. \"Likely\" fits: a stand-in reproduced the shape, and the receipts hold a read status and no body. The note separates what it shows from what it doesn't.\n\n2. Confirmed. `r2-enrol-a-new-2` reads GET, other, 404, and the third room's `enrol-checker` `new` reads 200. The S1 note's correction is right. Nothing shows where the 404 came from, and the note says so.\n\n3. No path through it signs or submits an act. In check mode, `advance` only settles, and `prepare` is never reached, since lines 302 and 309 return `prepared` first. A pending successor returns before anything is restored. A settled stage writes a new private row through `persist`, as `check` already does, and it adds to the chain and replaces no retained original. That rests on my reading, plus your controls `t1-no-act-on-recheck` and `t2-no-act-on-recheck`.\n\n4. Keep the recheck on a refusal. The second room's 404 is the only refused read on record, and its later `check` passed, so stopping at once would have stopped that room. Ten seconds is a small cost for a lasting refusal, and the receipt still gives the status.\n\n5. No, I found no way out of the table. `invitationCause` reads the reason only as a key, under `Object.hasOwn`, so an inherited name can't match, and `report` carries the word and a count. `diagnosticFetch` records method, category and status. An unlisted reason reads `unknown`. Note one small limit: `binding-unverified` is the word for any `unknown` state with no reason, and that is how the engine reports it today.\n\n## For the planner\n\nI recommend the request for the engine to wait for an active inbox. The page's agent-key flow can meet this stop, and only the engine can repair it. It is hosted code with a pinned hash, so it can follow the real room. The real room doesn't need it.\n\n## Checks at this head\n\n- The gate at d1af2197, tree 7114e67a, exits 0: Plain 3,240 with one skip, Native 901 with two skips. From there to this head, only the note, the manifest and the S1 note change.\n- `git merge-tree --write-tree` of c1ff846e and this head gives this head's tree.\n- The gate unit verifies: 36 files with none writable, and `SHA256SUMS` digest 041e2ee6. All 4 manifest rows match.\n- All 22 control logs say that they distinguish. I read that word in each and did not rerun them.\n- I ran `identities.test.ts` once, 11 of 11. `check-notes` gives 0 warnings, `check-doc-links` finds 780 links with 0 broken, `check-commit-messages` passes, and the worktree stayed clean.\n\nNo room has run the recheck, so whether 10 rechecks cover a real window is unknown, as the note says. No hosted code changes, and I ran no independent second read.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n- Architecture: approved in substance. The repair sits in the script, and the engine stays pinned until a request changes it.\n- Security: approved in substance. The cause is a fixed word, and no reason text, link or key reaches the receipt.\n- Simplification: approved. The table is one map and one function.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1ba7d1aaf39a0ac834408b11cf412bcfb0dd6d90","binding":"assigned","head":"73706bde555f941210035e708abbee2da001b60f","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f51231a18c695eeb6d25641eeb0256fd487b4629\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7b0de57d099ed98527db0f7120ce774e864163fc\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f51231a18c695eeb6d25641eeb0256fd487b4629","review_path":"reviewguard@1","stale":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:065bf926307bb71453935d7c628a7c998ab75dcb, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0d25d90aa03e3025b5dc28054ed18c522808d490, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:18c324706991a4a3e8c47476d6b35f378de4f9b8, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1ba7d1aaf39a0ac834408b11cf412bcfb0dd6d90, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:731ea0de10c5cd944dca2e72468fd41d0a24350b, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:906468561166c75e160ad36ac07b59d069aeec12, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ce6652398a08714568f103b7fd098776ba648784, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f51231a18c695eeb6d25641eeb0256fd487b4629, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:fd776bad50039c7e2fbb1804385c6461c5b78f3f stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:01e0dd696d953e8a4209c9e0a7461afc19c30b9a, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3